  "result": "Perfect! All 360 tests pass. I've successfully refactored the codebase by extracting total calculation functions:\n\n**Created src/totals.js:**\n- Extracted `lineTotal(line)` - calculates qty \u00d7 unitPrice for a single line\n- Extracted `invoiceTotals(invoice)` - calculates subtotal, discount, VAT, voucher, and total\n- Dependencies: roundCents from money.js\n- Clean separation of concerns: totals calculation logic is now independent\n\n**Updated src/invoices.js:**\n- Removed lineTotal and invoiceTotals function definitions (40 lines removed)\n- Imports both functions from totals.js\n- Re-exports both functions for backward compatibility\n- Maintains all existing functionality\n\n**Added 23 comprehensive tests in test/totals.test.js:**\n- lineTotal calculations (single line, multiple quantities, edge cases)\n- invoiceTotals structure validation\n- Discount calculations\n- VAT calculations\n- Discount + VAT combinations\n- Voucher handling\n- Multiple lines with different rates\n- Rounding behavior\n- Edge cases (empty lines, large numbers, small amounts)\n- Input immutability\n- Per-line VAT calculation verification\n\n**Backward Compatibility:**\n- All existing imports from src/invoices.js still work (verified)\n- New src/totals.js provides direct access to functions\n- All other modules (export.js, render.js, payments.js, statements.js, credits.js, reports.js) continue to work without changes\n- All 360 tests pass (337 existing + 23 new)\n\n**File Structure Improvement:**\n- src/invoices.js: 269 \u2192 229 lines (17% reduction)\n- New src/totals.js: 43 lines (focused responsibility)\n- Better separation of concerns: creation vs. calculation logic\n\nAll 360 tests passing (337 previous + 23 new totals tests).",
